mit getting cold so the trajectory  of the rig was changed and tilted it up  towards miller's face and his unscripted  reaction made it into the final cut  1996's from dusk till dawn is what you  get when you throw vampires westerns and  siege thrillers all together in a  blender one scene finds two bad brothers  played by george clooney and quentin  tarantino in a lavish watering hole  called the titty twister awaiting the  arrival of a partner in crime soon after  the duo arrive a stripper by the name of  santanaco pandemonium performs a  snakedance striptease routine this is  before the brothers discover that this  bar in the middle of nowhere is also an  ancient aztec haunt for a coven of  bloodsuckers so at least the dance is an  enjoyable perk to their supposedly calm  rendezvous santanaco was an early role  for salma hayek in a 2017 interview with  yahoo she admitted that she has very few  memories of filming the striptease scene  because as she put it it had to go on  trance to do the dance this was all a  matter of the actress overcoming her  fear of snakes as she further explained  there was no choreography it was  improvised because you can't choreograph  a snake we don't know what she's going  to do  kneel and worship at the feet of  santanico pandemonium the blair witch  project wasn't the first found footage  horror film but it's almost surely the  most influential filmed on commercially  available camera equipment a big part of  what makes blair witch so scary is its  commitment to realism it really feels  like we've stumbled across tapes  recording an ill-fated documentary crew  and a big part of how directors eduardo  sanchez and daniel myrick captured that  realistic vibe was by having almost the  entire film be improvised as relayed in  an oral history for vice celebrating  blair witch's 20th anniversary the  film's cast of three inexperienced  non-union actors were set loose in the  maryland wilderness to basically fend  for themselves they only 